## 3. Cyrillic & UTF-8 Encoding Protection
- Never use PowerShell `Set-Content`, `Out-File`, `echo`, or `>` / `>>` redirection without explicitly specifying `-Encoding utf8`. In Windows environments, standard redirection defaults to Windows-1251 (ANSI), destroying Cyrillic text.
- For automated file modifications or text manipulation involving Russian text, ALWAYS use Node.js scripts with explicit UTF-8 encoding (`fs.readFileSync(..., 'utf8')` / `fs.writeFileSync(..., 'utf8')`).

